  "before_interfaces": {
    "lem-discrete-one-step-error-recurrence-bound": [
      "## Statement\n\nLet $T>0$, $N\\ge1$, $h=T/N$, $p\\ge1$, and $C_0,C,L\\ge0$. If nonnegative real numbers $e_0,\\ldots,e_N$ satisfy\n$$e_0\\le C_0h^p,\\qquad e_{n+1}\\le(1+Lh)e_n+Ch^{p+1}\\quad(0\\le n<N),$$\nthen, when $L>0$,\n$$\\max_{0\\le n\\le N}e_n\\le\\left(C_0\\exp(LT)+C\\frac{\\exp(LT)-1}{L}\\right)h^p,$$\nand, when $L=0$,\n$$\\max_{0\\le n\\le N}e_n\\le(C_0+CT)h^p.$$"
    ],
    "thm-continuous-flow-log-density-equation": [
      "## Statement\n\nAssume the Axiom of Countable Choice. Let $d\\ge1$, $U_0\\subseteq\\mathbb R^d$ be open, $T>0$, and let $f$ be jointly $C^1$ on an open time-state domain. Suppose the ODE $x'(t)=f(t,x(t))$ has a common flow\n$$\\Phi:[0,T]\\times U_0\\to\\mathbb R^d,\\qquad x(t)=\\Phi_t(x_0),$$\nwhose time slices $\\Phi_t:U_0\\to U_t$ are $C^1$ diffeomorphisms onto open sets $U_t$, with $\\Phi_0=\\operatorname{id}_{U_0}$. Let $p_0:U_0\\to(0,\\infty)$ be a continuous probability density with respect to Lebesgue measure, let $\\mu_t$ be the pushforward of $p_0(x)\\,dx$ under $\\Phi_t$, and define\n$$p_t(y):=\\begin{cases}\\dfrac{p_0(\\Phi_t^{-1}(y))}{|\\det D\\Phi_t(\\Phi_t^{-1}(y))|},&y\\in U_t,\\\\0,&y\\notin U_t.\\end{cases}$$\nThen $p_t$ is a density of $\\mu_t$ on $\\mathbb R^d$, the flow Jacobian has positive determinant, and\n$$p_t(\\Phi_t(x_0))=\\frac{p_0(x_0)}{\\det D\\Phi_t(x_0)}>0,$$\nand, for $0<t<T$,\n$$\\frac{d}{dt}\\log p_t(x(t))=-\\operatorname{div}_x f(t,x(t)),\\qquad \\operatorname{div}_x f:=\\operatorname{tr}D_xf=\\sum_{i=1}^d\\partial_{x_i}f_i.$$\nThe derivative at $0$ or $T$ is understood one-sided."
    ],
    "thm-global-error-from-one-step-defect-and-stability": [
      "## Statement\n\nLet $d,N,p\\ge1$, $T>0$, $h=T/N$, and $t_n=nh$. Let $y:[0,T]\\to\\mathbb R^d$ solve an initial-value problem in an open time-state domain $D$. Use the Euclidean norm $\\|v\\|_2=(\\sum_{i=1}^d v_i^2)^{1/2}$ of [[def-euclidean-inner-product]], whose triangle inequality is proved in [[thm-cauchy-schwarz-and-the-euclidean-norm]]. Let $\\mathcal T\\subset D$ be a common compact time-state tube with positive margin in $D$, and write $\\mathcal T_t:=\\{v\\in\\mathbb R^d:(t,v)\\in\\mathcal T\\}$. Suppose a one-step map $\\Psi_{h,n}$ is defined on $\\mathcal T_{t_n}$, produces $y_{n+1}=\\Psi_{h,n}(y_n)$, and the entire exact path, all numerical grid states, and every method stage lie in $\\mathcal T$. If constants $C,C_0,L\\ge0$, independent of $N$ and $n$, satisfy\n$$\\|y_0-y(0)\\|_2\\le C_0h^p,\\qquad \\|\\Psi_{h,n}(y(t_n))-y(t_{n+1})\\|_2\\le Ch^{p+1},$$\nand\n$$\\|\\Psi_{h,n}(u)-\\Psi_{h,n}(v)\\|_2\\le(1+Lh)\\|u-v\\|_2$$\nfor every $u,v\\in\\mathcal T_{t_n}$ and $0\\le n<N$, then, for $L>0$,\n$$\\max_{0\\le n\\le N}\\|y_n-y(t_n)\\|_2\\le\\left(C_0\\exp(LT)+C\\frac{\\exp(LT)-1}{L}\\right)h^p,$$\nand, for $L=0$,\n$$\\max_{0\\le n\\le N}\\|y_n-y(t_n)\\|_2\\le(C_0+CT)h^p.$$"
    ],
    "thm-divergence-integral-error-with-separate-quadrature": [
      "## Statement\n\nLet $T>0$, $N\\ge1$, $h=T/N$, and $t_n=nh$. Let $K\\subseteq\\mathbb R^d$ be compact, let $x:[0,T]\\to K$ be an exact path, and suppose every numerical state $x_n$ also belongs to $K$. Let $q:[0,T]\\times K\\to\\mathbb R$ be a continuous scalar integrand. Define\n$$I_n:=\\int_{t_n}^{t_{n+1}}q(s,x(s))\\,ds,\\qquad \\ell_n:=\\ell_0+\\sum_{j=0}^{n-1}I_j.$$\nSuppose the one-step state method satisfies the hypotheses of [[thm-global-error-from-one-step-defect-and-stability]] at order $p\\ge1$, and write $K_x$ for its resulting constant, so $\\max_n\\|x_n-x(t_n)\\|_2\\le K_xh^p$. Let $Q_h(t_n,\\cdot):K\\to\\mathbb R$ be the increment map in the numerical scalar update $\\widehat\\ell_{n+1}=\\widehat\\ell_n+Q_h(t_n,x_n)$, with $|\\widehat\\ell_0-\\ell_0|\\le C_{\\ell,0}h^r$ for $r\\ge0$. If constants $K_q,D\\ge0$ and an integer $m\\ge1$ satisfy, uniformly for $n<N$ and $u,v\\in K$,\n$$|Q_h(t_n,u)-Q_h(t_n,v)|\\le hK_q\\|u-v\\|_2,\\qquad |Q_h(t_n,x(t_n))-I_n|\\le Dh^{m+1},$$\nthen\n$$\\max_{0\\le n\\le N}|\\widehat\\ell_n-\\ell_n|\\le C_{\\ell,0}h^r+TK_qK_xh^p+DT h^m.$$"
